# Welcome!

#### This professional learning module is designed to prepare you to teach Code.org's Thinking Critically About AI unit, part of the AI Discoveries curriculum. This curriculum is an engaging, hands-on dive into artificial intelligence, equipping students to evaluate AI-generated information, recognize its limitations, and apply thoughtful human judgment.

___


<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; width: 95%; margin: 20pt auto; padding: 0 5px;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/74f3ec76174ef6324dcf99cd83747c77-MS20.png"
       alt=""
       style="border-radius: 10px; width: 32%;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/39865d85d9b427a3d61825ec2b7b2a8d-MS23.png"
       alt=""
       style="border-radius: 10px; width: 32%;">
  <img src="https://images.code.org/94cdfab9f34af898f2dcefba81b8798a-image-1772147512323.47.44 PM.png"
       alt=""
       style="border-radius: 10px; width: 32%;">
</div>

___


#### By the end of this professional learning module, you will be able to:

* #### Articulate how human decisions can influence AI behavior, including issues of bias, privacy, credibility, and environmental impact.
* #### Guide students in analyzing AI outputs for accuracy, bias, safety, and ethical implications.
* #### Understand how Thinking Critically About AI models key Project Based Learning (PBL) elements such as sustained inquiry, critique and revision, student voice and choice, and public product development.

